  "claim_boundary": "The pinned repair source supplies twelve integer load coordinates. The integer radical of the repair-selected Gram is exactly the subgroup of antipodally equal loads, so its metric quotient is canonically the signed six-coordinate module. This removes the module as an independent algebraic input. The proper carrier action preserves the quotient, and the exact conditional mean intertwines with its induced operator. For the thirty source seams, composing the incidence boundary with the load quotient has rank six and image exactly the even-sum D6 lattice. Its direction axes bind to the existing edge30 control ray without making the seams spatial hops or nonlinear repair updates. For each positive protected total, differences of admissible source states generate the even-sum D6 lattice, whose repair-Gram image is dense in the same conditional three-dimensional completion. A fixed-total state set itself is finite and is not dense. The full nonlinear repair kernel does not descend through the quotient; an exact total-two counterexample is retained. Therefore ordered-history descent, operational position semantics, adoption of the repair clauses, cofinal gluing, global space, physical action, scale, prediction, and comparison remain open.",
